<%- include('partials/header', { title: 'About & API', active: 'about' }) %>

<h1>About</h1>
<p class="intro">This site is a personal blog, with an open board and a museum search built in.</p>

<section class="section">
  <h2>The board</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/board">board</a> is open to anyone. Write a title, sign it with any name, and post. New posts go to the top, and each post has its own page for comments.</p>
  <p>Posts are public. There are no profiles, likes, or notifications.</p>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Museum page</h2>
  <p>The <a href="/museum">Museum</a> page searches the public collection of the Art Institute of Chicago. Their API is free, needs no key, and returns real artwork data and images.</p>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <h2>Public API</h2>
  <p>Exposed Public API for getting a posts info and details. C:</p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Endpoint</th><th>Returns</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>GET /api/public/posts</code></td>
          <td>All posts with id, title, author, createdAt, and commentCount.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>GET /api/public/posts/:id</code></td>
          <td>One post with its body and comments.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <pre><code>fetch('/api/public/posts')
  .then((res) =&gt; res.json())
  .then((posts) =&gt; console.log(posts));</code></pre>
</section>

